#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186100593 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186101007 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "0e3833c1-4ec5-5681-ae69-6a9cceece871" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying the Slope and Y-Intercept From the Equation of a Line"}] :question/id #uuid "95fc8e7d-776c-5d09-9140-a83dc575ac79" :question/math-academy-id "e-12851" :question/problem "What are the slope and $y$-intercept of the line $y=2x-9$?" :question/worked-solution "The equation is in slope-intercept form\n\n$$\ny={\\color{red}{m}}x+{\\color{blue}{b}}\n$$\n\nwhere $\\color{red}{m}$ is the slope and $\\color{blue}{b}$ is the $y$-intercept.\n\nFor the equation $y=2x-9$, we see that the slope is\n\n$$\n{\\color{red}{m=2}}\n$$\n\nand the $y$-intercept is\n\n$$\n{\\color{blue}{b=-9}}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186100594 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186101008 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "d8e10b2d-cad1-5d50-b9fc-917c3367f814" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Equation of a Graphed Line (Positive Slope)"}] :question/id #uuid "36e13cef-f61a-53e2-8f0e-9ff567dc6fb6" :question/math-academy-id "e-12852" :question/problem "![](images/46/46a04d55edd836050d30a0d4d52c4c441619babd79f93f3540f61a5f437a1ea7.png)\n\nThe line shown above passes through the points $(0,-2)$ and $(2,2)$." :question/worked-solution "We will write the equation of the line in the slope-intercept form\n\n$$\ny=mx+b\n$$\n\nSo, we need to work out the slope $m$ and the $y$-intercept $b$.\n\nFrom the graph, we see that the line intercepts the $y$-axis at $(0,-2)$. So, the $y$-intercept is $b = -2$.\n\nWe can calculate the slope of the line by choosing two points on the line and applying the slope formula. The line passes through the points $(0,-2)$ and $(2,2)$, so we calculate its slope as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nm &= \\frac{y_{2} - y_{1}}{x_{2} - x_{1}} \\\\\n&= (2 - (-2))/(2 - 0) \\\\\n&= \\frac{4}{2} \\\\\n&= 2\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting the slope $m = 2$ and the $y$-intercept $b = -2$ into the slope-intercept form\n\n$$\ny = mx + b\n$$\n\nwe obtain the equation of the line:\n$y = 2x - 2$."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186100595 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186101010 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "4762cb71-f6b6-5d32-8d0b-a457db66ff97" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Equation of a Line That Passes Through Two Points: Y-Intercept Given"}] :question/id #uuid "8351e1cb-c602-5968-be5a-9c337ad977de" :question/math-academy-id "e-12853" :question/problem "Calculate the equation of the straight line that passes through the points $(0,8)$ and $(3,2)$." :question/worked-solution "We will write the equation of the line in the slope-intercept form\n\n$$\ny=mx+b\n$$\n\nSo, we need to work out the slope $m$ and the $y$-intercept $b$.\n\nFirst, we calculate the slope $m$ using the given points:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nm &= \\frac{y_{2} - y_{1}}{x_{2} - x_{1}} \\\\\n&= \\frac{2 - 8}{3 - 0} \\\\\n&= \\frac{-6}{3} \\\\\n&=-2\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe coordinates of the $y$-intercept are always $(0,{\\color{blue}{b}})$. We know that the line passes through the point $(0,{\\color{blue}{8}})$, so the $y$-intercept is\n\n$$\nb={\\color{blue}{8}}\n$$\n\nSubstituting the slope $m=-2$ and the $y$-intercept $b=8$ into the slope-intercept formula\n\n$$\ny=mx+b\n$$\n\nwe reach\n\n$$\ny=-2x+8\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186100617 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186101009 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "8ac060cb-0c76-5050-9156-e5f17ad26fbb" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Equation of a Graphed Line (Negative Slope)"}] :question/id #uuid "206b8f86-4184-50fa-9999-08700d10dc4f" :question/math-academy-id "e-20867" :question/problem "Find the equation of the line shown below.\n\n![](images/42/4298ec9c12555fd5e87265617ee274ef0fa859decd3ccd9473dfe8f778492df0.png)" :question/worked-solution "We will write the equation of the line in the slope-intercept form\n\n$$\ny=mx+b\n$$\n\nSo, we need to work out the slope $m$ and the $y$-intercept $b$.\n\nFrom the graph, we see that the line intercepts the $y$-axis at $(0,2)$. So, the $y$-intercept is $b=2$.\n\nWe can calculate the slope of the line by choosing two points on the line and applying the slope formula. The line passes through the points $(0,2)$ and $(6,0)$, so we calculate its slope as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nm &= \\frac{y_{2} - y_{1}}{x_{2} - x_{1}} \\\\\n&= \\frac{0 - 2}{6 - 0} \\\\\n&= \\frac{-2}{6} \\\\\n&=-\\frac{1}{3}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting the slope\n\n$$\nm=-\\dfrac{1}{3}\n$$\n\nand the $y$-intercept $b=2$ into the slope-intercept form\n\n$$\ny=mx+b\n$$\n\nwe obtain the equation of the line:\n\n$$\ny=-\\dfrac{1}{3}x+2\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186101240 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186101007 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "0e3833c1-4ec5-5681-ae69-6a9cceece871" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying the Slope and Y-Intercept From the Equation of a Line"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/id #uuid "64a16bc0-7e89-536a-a2fd-0afc037a1fba" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186098775} {:answer-field/id #uuid "78cde657-671c-56b7-936f-dbc0cf54fa26" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186098776}] :question/id #uuid "7a568a73-edca-58dd-acc8-ad4fc1b68903" :question/math-academy-id "q-171689" :question/problem "Determine the slope and $y$-intercept of the line $y = 4x - 3$.The slope of the line is\n{{field-1}}\nand the $y$-intercept is\n{{field-2}}."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186101260 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186101010 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "4762cb71-f6b6-5d32-8d0b-a457db66ff97" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Equation of a Line That Passes Through Two Points: Y-Intercept Given"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/id #uuid "e531a471-fcee-5258-89f1-728bfe52aaca" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186098886}] :question/id #uuid "c0b425fb-b8a2-5723-acb7-016f2e613ac7" :question/math-academy-id "q-179507" :question/problem "Written in the form $y = mx + b$, what is the equation of the line that passes through the points $(3,-10)$ and $(0,-4)$?The equation of the line is $y =$\n{{field-1}}."}]}
